+
+## Ready-action focus continuity
+
+Find, Review and original-file preparation disable their initiating action while work runs. Native inspection of the preceding candidate found that both Find and Review left focus on the document body. This happened with an empty origin and with a discovered `release-v0.60.3` profile; it is not limited to empty results.
+
+The separate correction gives each operation its explicit initiating control. If that control currently owns foreground focus, it transfers focus synchronously to the available Cancel action before awaiting the read. Empty or failed Find returns from Cancel to Find; a successful Find with channels moves to Review. Other checks return to their still-available initiating action. A prepared export retains the existing explicit download-link handoff. Newer focus wins, a background start cannot take focus, and background cancellation invalidates a deferred return even if the page becomes foreground before the read settles. Closing the view prevents all completion handoffs. No automatic Find, storage write, new router or new data capability is introduced.
+
+The full four-patch composition on exact `a13ab970222498d7c5fa7f62f9fc04fe436979d5` passes **89/89 tests on Node 20.19.5 and 89/89 on Node 22.22.2**, using the same six complete affected files sequentially at 1024 MiB. All 95 inputs / 1,152,610 bytes remain unchanged across each run. The preceding ready-view runtime fails seven cases in the two complete view files (26 pass / 7 fail). These regressions use the actual view and model the observed browser behavior in which disabling the focused control moves focus to the body. Reader results, original verification and download handles are fixture boundaries; they do not establish real browser file recovery, physical input or corrected native focus painting. Earlier 68/76/81 cohorts and packets remain unchanged; native correction acceptance is still pending.
